menu "cli: command shell"

    config CLI_MAX_GROUPS
        int "Maximum registered command groups"
        default 32
        range 4 128
        help
            Groups are registered at startup by the application and by any
            component that ships commands. The table holds pointers only; the
            groups themselves stay static const in the modules that define them.

    config CLI_MAX_LINE_LEN
        int "Maximum command line length (bytes)"
        default 256
        range 64 1024

    config CLI_MAX_ARGS
        int "Maximum tokens in a command line"
        default 32
        range 4 128
        help
            Includes the group token. A line with more tokens is truncated by
            the tokenizer, not rejected.

    config CLI_HISTORY_LEN
        int "Command history entries"
        default 32
        range 0 128

    config CLI_COMMAND_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Pending commands queued for the executor"
        default 4
        range 1 32
        help
            Every interface -- serial, web -- queues here, and one task drains
            it, so commands never run concurrently. Depth only covers bursts;
            it does not add parallelism.

    config CLI_EXECUTOR_STACK
        int "Executor task stack (bytes)"
        default 6144
        range 2048 32768
        help
            Every command runs on this task, including I2C scans and WiFi
            operations, so it needs more stack than a typical worker.

    config CLI_READER_STACK
        int "Serial reader task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384

endmenu
